# Operators

## Arithmetic

The arithmetic operators `+`, `-`, `*`, and `/` operate element-wise on arrays with the same axis lengths: `a + b` adds each element of `a` to the corresponding element of `b`.

When one operand is a scalar, the operation is applied between the scalar and every element of the array, as in `2*a - 1`.

Assignment operators, like `+=` or `*=`, combine an operation with an assignment.

